// TryCatch rtype orphan (aug05g hz0 divergence_000000, hand-reduced):
// TryCatch::new snapshotted the last try-body node's type at
// CONSTRUCTION, but a select body REPLACES its typ field during
// typecheck0 (the arm union), so the snapshot held the select's
// orphaned pre-typecheck tvar cell — unbound forever, and
// contains(Number, orphan) bound it at the use site, admitting
// i64 + struct through the try/catch wrapper (the bare select and the
// explicit union annotation both rejected correctly). The interp then
// reached the Value-level broadcast add ruled unreachable-from-typed-
// code (nested "can't add error types" garbage); the jit produced
// nothing. Third instance of the orphan-snapshot family (jul08o
// nested-select, the Sample snapshot). Fix: TryCatch::typ() DELEGATES
// live to the last try-body node — this program must CompileErr-agree
// in both modes.
{let s = { catch(e) i64:42; select i64:100 {i64:42 => { b: f64:1., y: i64:2 }, _ => { b: f64:0., y: i64:42 }} }; i64:0 + s}
